title: "Account for the extrinsic length in the proof_size weight dimension"

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Previously the encoded length of an extrinsic was handled separately from its `Weight`: it was
    passed around as an extra `len` parameter and `CheckWeight` added it to the `proof_size`
    dimension manually. Any transaction extension that forgot this subtlety would under-account the
    proof size.

    The extrinsic length is now treated as a first class part of the extrinsic weight. `DispatchInfo`
    gains a new `length_weight: Weight` field which carries the `proof_size` contribution of the
    encoded extrinsic. The FRAME executive fills it in before running the transaction extension
    pipeline, so `DispatchInfo::total_weight()` already includes the length and every extension
    receives the correct total proof size automatically.

    Consequently:
    - `DispatchInfo::total_weight()` now returns `call_weight + extension_weight + length_weight`.
    - The post-dispatch actual weight (re-assembled in `dispatch_transaction`) now also re-adds the
      non-reclaimable length weight, so unspent-weight reclaim never reclaims the extrinsic length.
    - `frame_system::Pallet::reclaim_weight` no longer needs the extrinsic length passed in.
    - `frame_system::calculate_consumed_weight`, `calculate_consumed_extrinsic_weight` and
      `CheckWeight::do_prepare` no longer take a `len` argument as the length is already part of
      `DispatchInfo`.

    Block length enforcement (`CheckWeight::check_block_length`) is unchanged and still uses the raw
    extrinsic length.

    Closes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/9410.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    On runtimes that price the `proof_size` weight dimension, the weight reported for an extrinsic
    (and the corresponding weight-based fee) now includes the encoded length of the extrinsic in the
    `proof_size` dimension. The total cost of an extrinsic is unchanged in intent; the length is now
    accounted as weight instead of being handled separately. Runtimes that do not price `proof_size`
    in `WeightToFee` (the common `ref_time`-only case) are unaffected.

crates:
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: patch
- name: frame-system
  bump: major
- name: frame-executive
  bump: patch
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-pallet-weight-reclaim
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-storage-weight-reclaim
  bump: patch
# The following crates only construct `DispatchInfo` in tests/benchmarks; they gain the new
# `length_weight` field with its default value and have no functional change.
- name: pallet-transaction-payment
  bump: none
- name: pallet-asset-tx-payment
  bump: none
- name: pallet-asset-conversion-tx-payment
  bump: none
- name: pallet-bridge-relayers
  bump: none
